  "result": "The gate never judged my files. All three runs returned **SCOPE_VIOLATION**, and none of the files it flagged are ones I edited. It listed files under `.runtime/tmp/claude-154266/…`: the agent runtime's background-task output files, some belonging to other sessions (LVMC-11-18-020, LVMC-11-30-050), plus a `cache-break-state-*.json`. The runtime adds one of these for every shell call, so more runs could only fail the same way. I stopped with 3 of the 6 runs used. The harness needs to leave `.runtime/` out of its scope check, or put that temp folder outside the repo.\n\nTwo of those three runs were my mistakes: one ran the unedited skeleton files, and one I started by accident while trying to read a file. Another command that wasn't the gate was blocked because the session can't approve anything.\n\n**What's in the files:**\n- **Rule:** the subject must be a `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`. The rule applies when the subject enters a roundabout region `r` (it is inside `r` now and wasn't at the observation before). The duty holds for every vehicle that was in `r` both before and at that entry: the subject must not touch it. And the two cars' centres must not come, at constant velocities, within `p.conflict_centre_clearance` of each other inside `p.conflict_horizon`. The duty repeats the same choice of `r`. I declared no narrowings of the reading.\n- **Witnesses:** I built the five planned scenes (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_1) and added two of my own. branch_2 has a bicycle on the conflicting course, which isn't a vehicle under the definition. branch_3 has a car entering at the same moment from another side, so it wasn't already in the roundabout. Both expect compliant. Each scene clears the 3 s / 3 m reading by a wide margin; for example, forbid's closest approach is about 2.1 m and permit's about 30 m.\n\n**Likely problem in the node:** span b6 claims `kin.speed`, but the node's own duty never uses speed. Once the scope check is fixed, the gate will probably return UNUSED_CLAIM on it. The plan agent should either drop `kin.speed` from b6 or say in the duty what the speed does.\n\n`task_result.md` in the working directory records each run, these choices, and the node issue.",
